{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PointMesh"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The PointMesh is made from a single point. Instead of relying on triangles, points are rendered as a single rectangle on the screen with a constant size. They are intended to be used with Particle systems, but can be used as a cheap way to render constant size billboarded sprites (for example in a point cloud).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"PointMeshes, must be used with a material that has a point size. Point size can be accessed in a shader with ","type":"text"},{"code":"POINT_SIZE","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or in a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/BaseMaterial3D","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" by setting ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/BaseMaterial3D\/usePointSize","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and the variable ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/BaseMaterial3D\/pointSize","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When using PointMeshes, properties that normally alter vertices will be ignored, including billboard mode, grow, and cull face."}]}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Mesh with a single Point primitive.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:10SwiftGodot9PointMeshC","symbolKind":"class","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PointMesh","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"SwiftGodot"}],"roleHeading":"Class","role":"symbol","title":"PointMesh","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind